## 📦 Installation

### Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/website-auditor.git
cd website-auditor
```

---

## Backend Setup

Navigate to the backend folder.

```bash
cd backend
```

Install dependencies.

```bash
npm install
```

Start the server.

```bash
npm run dev
```

The backend runs on

```
http://localhost:5000
```

---

## Frontend Setup

Open another terminal.

```bash
cd frontend
```

Install dependencies.

```bash
npm install
```

Run the development server.

```bash
npm run dev
```

The frontend runs on

```
http://localhost:5173
```

---

## API Endpoint

### POST

```
/api/audit
```

### Request

```json
{
  "url": "https://example.com"
}
```

---

## Successful Response

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "report": {
    "httpStatus": 200,
    "responseTime": "285 ms",
    "pageTitle": "Example Domain",
    "metaDescription": "Example website description",
    "h1Count": 1,
    "imagesWithoutAlt": 0,
    "approximateWordCount": 250
  }
}
```

---

## Error Responses

### Invalid URL

```json
{
  "success": false,
  "message": "Invalid URL"
}
```

### Missing URL

```json
{
  "success": false,
  "message": "URL is required"
}
```

### Timeout

```json
{
  "success": false,
  "message": "Request timed out"
}
```

### Non-HTML Response

```json
{
  "success": false,
  "message": "Response is not HTML"
}
```

---

## 📊 Audit Metrics

The application reports the following:

| Metric | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| HTTP Status | HTTP status code returned by the server |
| Response Time | Time taken to fetch the webpage |
| Page Title | HTML `<title>` element |
| Meta Description | Meta description tag content |
| H1 Count | Number of `<h1>` elements |
| Images Missing Alt | Images without an `alt` attribute |
| Approximate Word Count | Estimated number of words on the page |

---

## ⚠️ Error Handling

The application safely handles:

- Invalid URLs
- Missing URLs
- Request timeouts
- Network failures
- Non-HTML responses
- Unreachable websites

The server always returns meaningful JSON responses and avoids crashes.

